    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/desmopuntius_hexazona_wild_en/",
      "html": "<p>Like all Desmopuntius they should be kept in schools.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/desmopuntius_hexazona_wild_en/",
      "html": "<p>The banded barbs from Southeast Asia were always matters of interest, both of aquarists and scientists. The generic position of the species was unclear for quite a long time: they were placed in Barbus, Puntius, or Systomus. But it seems that the problem has been solved finally. The elongated species are now placed in the genus Desmopuntius (species: D. endecanalis, D. foerschi, D. gemellus, D. hexazona, D. johorensis, D. pentazona, D. rhomboocellatus, and D. trifasciatus), the deep bodied species (\"tiger barbs\") in Puntigrus (species: P. anchisporus, P. navjotsodhii, P. partipentazona, P. pulcher, and P. tetrazona).</p>"
    }
  ],
